WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.770
By the way let me help you guys

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.480
understand something because sometimes

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.639
people don't. The Gazelle intensity where

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:13.620
you're on beans and rice rice and beans,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.480
where you do not have a life, you do not

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.850
go on vacation, you do not do anything. Is until you get out of debt and you finish

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.609
baby step 3. When you have your emergency

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:25.500
fund in place and your debt free except

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.470
your home that's when you lighten up a

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.570
notch. You let the foot off the gas a

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.329
little bit and you start to live.

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:34.680
That's when you save up and go on a

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.050
vacation or you save up and pay for a

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.480
couch or you save up and move up and

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.000
home or you save up and pay cash for a

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.410
little better car because you're driving

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.920
a hoopty or whatever and hopefully you

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.719
can do that while you're saving fifteen

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:50.579
percent towards retirement, if you can't

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:52.559
then you knock a couple of those little

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:54.420
things out to get your lifestyle back up

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.070
to a reasonable level and then you

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.350
then you start baby steps four because

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.809
baby step four, five and six (which is

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:02.280
fifteen percent of your income going

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:09.270
into retirement and baby step 5

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:12.600
is kids college and six is paying off

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.760
your home early) those are done you know

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.720
over a period of years, you know. And it's

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.200
part of your overall goal. So here's the

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.540
thing I read this thing somebody tweeted

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.000
me earlier today. It's lady said I quit

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.009
doing Dave Ramsey so I could save my

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:32.100
marriage. And when I read the article it

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.049
was like you know she was till gazelle

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:35.579
intense and trying to pay off her house

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:37.950
and her husband hated her and

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.840
hated me and everything else because they were

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.909
still, you know, they're still just living

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:43.829
on beans and rice five, six, seven years

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:47.189
later. And that is not what we teach and

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:49.290
so you can't say you quit doing Dave

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.030
Ramsey because honey you weren't doing

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.430
Dave Ramsey. You weren't doing what we

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:57.270
teach. And you did what you wanted to do

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.759
and you blame me for it but that's not

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:01.890
what we teach. We don't teach people to

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.079
do that and nor would I teach you to do

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:07.020
something to end your marriage, that's

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.009
just absolutely drama queen stuff. You've

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:12.870
never heard that here on the air. I tell

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:13.800
people to do things

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.190
keep their marriage together.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.160
If you go into hyper drama mode

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.500
for a decade like that and your spouse

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.930
is not on board, that's not me giving

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.520
your marriage problems, that's you giving

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.010
you marriage problems. You know that's

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:34.410
not what we teach. So baby steps 1, 2 &amp;

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.900
3 are with great focused intensity

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.690
extreme levels of sacrifice and even

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.190
then your spouse needs to be on board

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.230
because it's not going to work you're

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.910
just going to make everybody mad around

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.740
when you try to force this stuff upon

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.810
them but when it is a shared goal we're

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.250
sacrificing to win. We're going to live

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.990
like no one else so later we can live

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.390
and give like no one else. Then when you

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.760
break through baby step 3, you have your

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.230
emergency fund in place, you don't have

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.030
any payments but a house payment that

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.800
puts you in a place to be able to save

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.260
and invest and be able to do some

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.880
lifestyle things and be able to increase

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.400
your giving and get yourself in a rhythm

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.550
that is much more reasonable long-term.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.090
And still be able to hit the goals. It

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.490
still happens and you still have to be

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.250
focused, you still have to be a grown-up but

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.959
I'm amazed the number of things I get

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:24.120
blamed for that I didn't do. This is The

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.940
Dave Ramsey Show. Hey guys thanks for

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.190
watching if you enjoyed this video click

